<title>USA: Franklin to buy Insilco Rolodex unit.</title>
<headline>Franklin to buy Insilco Rolodex unit.</headline>
<dateline>BURLINGTON, N.J. 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franklin Electronic Publishers Inc said Friday it has agreed to buy Insilco Corp's Rolodex Electronics unit for an undisclosed amount in cash.</p>
<p>The agreement gives Franklin the right to build and market a variety of electronics products under the Rolodex Electronic brand name, it said.</p>
<p>The company said it expects to create products for the line and to integrate its Bookman memory card technology into Rolodex Electronic organizers.</p>
<p>Insilco is based in Columbus, Ohio.  </p>
<p>In a statement released Friday afternoon, Insilco said the deal was worth about $16 million after transaction costs.</p>
